{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1114673-describing-awakenings","id":1114673,"title":"Describing Awakenings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T11:01:54-07:00","id":1114673,"title":"Describing Awakenings?","content":"Where in the M20 book does it have guidelines on running a Mage's awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T11:02:41-07:00","id":1114674,"title":"","content":"And how would YOU do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:46:59-07:00","id":1115091,"title":"","content":"While I don't believe M20 has details on _running_ an awakening (since it assumes that starting characters have been mages for a while), Initiates of the Art is a whole book dedicated to the newly awakened.<br /> <br /> That said, given how personal an individual's awakening is (and practically no two are alike), I would run it as a session zero with the player describing the events that lead up to his/her awakening (i.e. little to no dice rolling and let the player make all of the important decisions, but the GM prompts important questions / conflicts for the player to decide).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12655-tzizimine","name":"tzizimine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T08:26:50-07:00","id":1115099,"title":"","content":"It's mostly described as an awareness. Whether that awareness comes from understanding scientific principles. or seeing a mystical world. Or even just having some mind melting Revelation during sex drugs and alcohol day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:26:55-07:00","id":1115941,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a theme in revised core book that tradition members who awaken are usually brought to it gently by a primer or the actions of an awakened mentor (possibly after an apprenticeship as a cult member or linear mage) while orphans usually awaken at times of extreme stress. They can always try and join a tradition later ;-)<br /> I ran an orphan awakening a short while ago which is mentioned in the thread I started (newbies campaign etc) where the players are sleepers caught on a tram in a shootout between a marauder and the technocracy. Their avatars manifested effects to save their lives and they were immediately knocked out by a paradox backlash. The heightened awareness came later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T13:18:39-07:00","id":1116079,"title":"","content":"Mage the Awakening dealt with this issue head on and in a manner that has stuck with me, so, to my mind, probably better than most Ascension material has handled it (which from the above seems to be the usual contradictory, mutli-editiion hydra-headed monster ham-handed mishmash that all too often comes about with Mage the Awakneing). <br /> <br /> The made a distinction that could be made on a game by game or character by character basis between Awakenings that occur in some sort of other-worldly never-never and those where the enlightenment comes from some degree of interaction with the material/real world with added dimensionality.<br /> <br /> The first kind are pure dreamscape. They are sorta hard to manage in terms of where the character actually is while it's going on. Are they just drooling on the couch? Do they disappear entirely? How overt is said disappearance? Is a clandestine no-one else is around Avatar kidnapping or do they just go &quot;POP&quot; and go to some kinda of reverse-wraithly-Harrowing in a not-place along the imaginary axis of the Tellurian (maybe the negative values of that axis are where the Paradox Realms are located?). There are definitely advantages to this sort of Awakening (and, later on, Seeking) in that it's purely a narrative by which the Avatar and the mage get to hash things out. It can be transforming your childhood home into a funhouse with mirrors depicting other versions of yourself based on alternative choices, leading up to this Choice, the BIG One, right now! Or it can be be what looks like an individual session where the character has to save Space Station Alpha from shutting down by reparing the reactor by which I mean enlightening his or her own soul. And so on. Practically, it means everyone being willing to play a session about A character and not the group (for which it, like a Harrowing, is a great idea to give the other players somethining important to do... Hey Chris, will you represent his ambition and lack of tact personified by his older brother?). Or doing it through cut-aways. <br /> <br /> The other way is for the meaning to get layered onto something that is manifestly going on in the game world. It can be really thin. Perhaps making the ham radio work by REALLY REALLY understanding it in a deep and meaningful way that is sort of like a prolonged Eureka moment. Or it can be thick, like reinterpreting what's going on in a more phantasmagorical way.... The house is a castly The car is the Black Coach. The homeless people are goblins. Whatever. <br /> <br /> The way Mage has been structured is a bit schizoid with regard to Awakenings. There's some feeling that people Awaken in the bosom of whatever Sect they later belong to. That seems to be the way the rules about character creation are sorta built. But the narrative of the game is pretty much that everyone who Awakens is a Orphan, it's a sudden unexpected and unpredictable thing (even when you have people with Time 2 all over the place), it usually results in a sort of mad grab of different groups trying to get the new-minted Mage first and then hammering some Practice and Instruments associated with their Sect down their throat. (Or, if they are being nice, seeing if their way of doing things is a good fit, and, if not, passing them off to whatever Sect in their Faction works better). Sure, there are probably some examples of people carefully nurtured in a Practice by a Mage who happen to Awaken and none of that jarring and upsetting unpleasantness happens to, but it seems like it's the exception, the rare exception, rather than the rule. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:23:05-07:00","id":1120100,"title":"","content":"Exemple of awakenings are also described in the short novels at the begining of the suppl. books or inside them in short stories between chapters (best exemple in mind, the book of Tradition : Cult of Ecstasy revised). In my chronicle, The easiest way to describe it is the new level of conciousness reached after traumatic events. Traumatic do not necessary means horrific or terrifying, it can also mean joyful or transcending.<br /> <br /> Awakenings can also be prepared. That way, I find it easier to describe them as new levels of understanding after an important experience or moment in a chantry or doing somehting with a mentor (a Son of Ether apprentice finishing an important calculus, a transcendental dance performed by a group of Verbena and young witches, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T05:28:14-07:00","id":1120758,"title":"","content":"Except that the conceits of the game work against most (but defnitely not all) of those stories.<br /> <br /> If mentors are aware of potential Awakenings and are on hand to guide the newbies, then Awakenings are predictable. Which we are told they are not. Not even in a world with Prime and Time and such available. The &quot;classic&quot; Awakening narrative is: Person Awakens with no warning. Factions swoop in to try to grab up the newbie before anyone else can get them. Faction uses its version of the Sorting Hat to assign them to an appropriate Sect, or, is dickish and does not and tries to cram the snowflake shaped ur-Orphan into whatever shaped hole that is this particular group.. The doings of Avatars are, apparently, mysterious things and unknowable to mere mortals. <br /> <br /> In addition, we are given a split conceit of exactly what you say - Sects (some Sects) are on the lookout for potentials and grab them up beforehand and then pre-train them in their whatever-it-is-that-differentiates-one-Sect-from-another-that-isn't-Focus-because-that's-personal/uber-Focus/old Mage &quot;Paradigm&quot; and then some fraction of them pop and become true mages and the rest (or a few or some of the rest) become Hedge Mages. But, we are told that, because of the unknowabillity of Awakenings as per above, this system isn't really reliable enough to act as the primary recruitment tool. (Then that is ignored. Then the ignoring of it is ignored.)<br /> <br /> It's also important to note that fiction pieces, while great to read, lack all agency in the sense that PCs usually have. Unless the Awakening lucks into one of these narratives by chance of synergy between the ST and the PC's interactions, trying to create these situations will pretty much be telling the PC what their Awakening is like, just as if they are reading some short fiction about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:58:48-07:00","id":1123586,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the argument is about my post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> . I will answer as if it was the case (or at least part of it) since it just follows it.<br /> <br /> I do not think you can play Mage and casually say &quot;this is not possible&quot;. Awakenings are what you want them to be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, the lore states multiple times that Awakenings can be prepared even if they cannot be actually triggered. I never said the Awakening was predictable. I just said some poeple with potential can be prepared for it. That does not mean they will Awaken. It means that sometimes, Mages will see a possibility and will train the concerned person to the point where he/she will Awaken... or not. Having occasions and opportunities does not mean someone will Awaken. However, it can slightly increase the probability of Awakening. &quot;Slightly&quot; is the keyword here. It can be enough to spend the time on it with the End of Times coming.<br /> <br /> You can find one of my prefered short stories of Mage at the begining of the Cult of Ecstasy tradition book. In the story, A Mage dreams about the love of her life. She searches for her and meet her when the concerned woman is still not Awakened. She dreamt about it, so the situation is complicated since the possibility exists that she will never Awaken. Therefore, she train her until the point when she creates the perfect moment for her Awakening and wait for the thing to happen... or not. I find the story beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}